<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jamaican Maroons</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Maroons of Jamaica</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jamaican <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maroons">Maroons</a> are descendants of Africans who escaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>, many during the English conquest of the island from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1655, and founded free communities in the mountains. After the First Maroon War the British signed treaties with them in 1739 and 1740, recognising their freedom and land. Some were deported to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-maroon-war">Second Maroon War</a> of 1795 to 1796.</p></div>
